-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 4 (Minimum Qualifying Period): regulation 13.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- "Qualifying year" is the 2014 Act's (section 2(4)); whether a given tax year is one is a fact about the person's
-- contribution record, so the number of qualifying years is a plain input here.

§ `Part 4 -- Minimum Qualifying Period`

-- src:142 | (1) For the purposes of section 2(3) of the 2014 Act (entitlement to state pension at full or reduced rate), the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the reduced rate is ten.
@ref Regulation 13(1) (src:142)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the reduced rate` MEANS 10

-- src:143 | (2) For the purposes of section 4(2) of the 2014 Act (entitlement to a state pension at transitional rate), the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the transitional rate is ten.
@ref Regulation 13(2) (src:143)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the transitional rate` MEANS 10

@ref Regulation 13(1) (src:142)
GIVEN `the number of qualifying years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person has the minimum number of qualifying years for the reduced rate` `the number of qualifying years` MEANS
    `the number of qualifying years` AT LEAST `the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the reduced rate`

@ref Regulation 13(2) (src:143)
GIVEN `the number of qualifying years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person has the minimum number of qualifying years for the transitional rate` `the number of qualifying years` MEANS
    `the number of qualifying years` AT LEAST `the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the transitional rate`
